{"name":"Cold Brew Coffee","hex":"#785736","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cold brew coffee","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["coffee, the liquid drink, which was created by steeping grounds in unheated water for hours (usually 12-24 hours) and then filtering out the grounds","a serving of such"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cold_brew_coffee"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cold brew coffee","blocks":[{"text":"Cold brew coffee, also called cold water extraction or cold pressing, is a type of coffee prepared by the process of steeping coffee grounds in water at cool temperatures for an extended period. Coarse-ground beans are soaked in water for 12 to 24 hours."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Preparation_of_cold_brew_coffee_06.jpg/330px-Preparation_of_cold_brew_coffee_06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cold_brew_coffee"},{"title":"Coffee preparation","blocks":[{"text":"Coffee preparation is the process of making liquid coffee using coffee beans. While the particular steps vary with the type of coffee and with the raw materials, the process includes four basic steps: raw coffee beans must be roasted, the roasted coffee beans must then be ground, and the ground coffee must then be mixed with hot or cold water for a specific time (brewed), the liquid coffee extraction must be separated from the used grounds, and finally, if desired, the extracted coffee is combined with other elements of the desired beverage, such as sweeteners, dairy products, dairy alternatives, or toppings."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/TEDxAMS2011_044.JPG/330px-TEDxAMS2011_044.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffee_preparation"},{"title":"Cold","blocks":[{"text":"Cold is the presence of low temperature, especially in the atmosphere. In common usage, cold is often a subjective perception. A lower bound to temperature is absolute zero, defined as 0.00 K on the Kelvin scale, an absolute thermodynamic temperature scale. This corresponds to −273.15 °C on the Celsius scale, −459.67 °F on the Fahrenheit scale, and 0.00 °R on the Rankine scale."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Antarctic_iceberg%2C_2001_-2.jpg/330px-Antarctic_iceberg%2C_2001_-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cold"},{"title":"Coffee","blocks":[{"text":"Coffee is a beverage brewed from roasted, ground coffee beans. Dark-colored and bitter, coffee has a stimulating effect on humans due to its caffeine content; however decaffeinated coffee is also commercially available. There are also various coffee substitutes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Latte_and_dark_coffee.jpg/330px-Latte_and_dark_coffee.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffee"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Nitro_Cold_Brew.jpg/500px-Nitro_Cold_Brew.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Nitro_Cold_Brew.jpg/1280px-Nitro_Cold_Brew.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Nitro_Cold_Brew.jpg/500px-Nitro_Cold_Brew.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Nitro cold brew","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANitro_Cold_Brew.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Interieur%2C_cycloon-machine_-_Hilversum_-_20346981_-_RCE.jpg/500px-Interieur%2C_cycloon-machine_-_Hilversum_-_20346981_-_RCE.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaig